🚽 Test case: #193 -- passing a struct-returning call result whose type
🚽 does not match the parameter (`show(mk())` where `mk` returns a `gang
🚽 Other` but `show` wants a `gang Point`) is rejected, and the temporary
🚽 return blob is released cleanly (no leak).
gang Point {
    rizz x;
};
gang Other {
    rizz z;
};

gang Other mk() {
    gang Other o;
    o.z = 1;
    bussin o;
}

skibidi show(gang Point p) {
    yapping("%d", p.x);
}

skibidi main {
    show(mk());
}
